# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Market data
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and edit. Restart `npm run dev` after a change.
#
# VITE_DATA_PROVIDERS — comma-separated, tried IN ORDER for every symbol. The
# first provider that can serve a symbol is used; if it fails (rate limit,
# unknown symbol, network) the next one takes over. Search asks all of them at
# once and merges the results. Symbols are TradingView-style ids, e.g.
# NASDAQ:AAPL, BINANCE:BTCUSDT, FX:EURUSD, SP:SPX, COMEX:GC1!.
#
# Available providers:
#
#   yahoo        Yahoo Finance — stocks, ETFs, indices, forex, futures, crypto.
#                No key. Live prices are POLLED (~5 s); some exchanges are
#                15-min delayed. Runs through the Vite dev/preview server
#                (/api/market/yahoo), so it does NOT work on a static host.
#                Unofficial API: Yahoo often rate-limits an IP (HTTP 429); the
#                next provider then takes over automatically.
#
#   binance      Binance spot — every BINANCE:<PAIR> (e.g. BINANCE:BTCUSDT).
#                No key, no server needed (called straight from the browser),
#                REAL-TIME best bid/ask over websocket. Crypto only. Not
#                available from some jurisdictions.
#
#   tradingview  TradingView's own feed via the unofficial
#                Mathieu2301/TradingView-API library (@mathieuc/tradingview).
#                Any EXCHANGE:TICKER TradingView knows; streaming quotes.
#                Runs in the Vite dev/preview server (/api/market/tv) because it
#                needs a websocket Origin header browsers can't set.
#                Caveats: not an official API and may break whenever TradingView
#                changes its protocol; using it may conflict with TradingView's
#                Terms of Use — your responsibility. Anonymous access gets
#                limited intraday history and may be delayed.
#
#   demo         Bundled offline history for 6 crypto pairs and a simulated
#                tick stream. Use it ALONE (VITE_DATA_PROVIDERS=demo) for
#                offline work, CI or a static-host deploy.
#
VITE_DATA_PROVIDERS=yahoo,binance,tradingview

# Optional, tradingview provider only: your TradingView session cookies
# (`sessionid` and `sessionid_sign` from tradingview.com in your browser) for
# the data your account can access. SERVER-ONLY — deliberately not VITE_-
# prefixed so they never reach the browser bundle. Never commit them.
TV_SESSIONID=
TV_SESSIONID_SIGN=
